+
+A bounded peer audit on unchanged source
+`8105b0c6704d022567a9681768c76fc3624d3be5c300b1b941a9fbc1494cf104`
+found a new candidate outside the 17 declared rivals. With seed 2, easy difficulty,
+and consecutive sample indices 1..4, the first three source boxes are square
+3x3, while the query source box is 3x2. Clockwise rotation preserving the source
+box's bottom-left corner agrees with all three demonstration outputs but shifts
+the query result down one row. Eight protected Racket executions confirmed all
+three demonstration matches and six differing query cells; all four inputs pass
+the current ordinary and strict-canonical validators. The current lesson hook
+returns no reasons because this corner-anchor rival is not declared.
+
+Reproduce with `counterexamples/corner_anchor_review/probe.py`; the exact programs,
+four-pair witness, source binding and runtime identity are in
+`WORK/checks/9d2f7c9e2ac4/corner-anchor-result.json`, with its executed command in
+`WORK/checks/9d2f7c9e2ac4/corner-anchor-command.json`. This is one direct-generator
+window, not a new materializer census or prevalence estimate. The upper worked
+analogy supports top-left anchoring; the tested candidate, like the fixed
+canonical program, preserves that context without applying its lower-panel rule
+to it. Follow-up should assess this candidate and add non-square demonstration
+coverage and corner-anchor rivals if warranted. Generator, rule and approval
+state remain unchanged; the finding remains open.
 
